@startuml frontend_debug_header_flow
' Frontend pre-change baseline: origin/main dee709fc584dd722d2e94eb381338b997659e35a.
' Synced main baseline: origin/main a7a245b4079b53f79eacb96475a1b58a9c3713c7; ADR-0033 was already allocated.
' Backend feature commit: d03c08dbae870f19eee8d4fa79a707185f7a26b5, merged before the frontend baseline.
' Observed source: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts (requestRaw generated non-secret X-HW-ID and had no custom header input).
' Observed source: frontend/src/components/DevDiagnostics.vue (the only pre-change development tool entry).
' Backend source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java (submit).
' Backend source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeRequestContext.java (mateCredentials).
' Backend source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/client/HttpMateToolClient.java (invokeTool).
' Initial reviewed implementation: eb347db8c13eda13c240dc4cf60154fc49b9bd91.
' Initial reviewed source: frontend/src/components/DebugHeaders.vue (snapshot) and frontend/src/debugHeaders.ts (validateDebugHeaders).
' Initial reviewed source: frontend/src/App.vue (submit) and frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts (sendMessage and mergeRequestHeaders).
' Review correction implementation: 3b3e51f13f7a97cf1b135d13f4b1285e147c74ae.
' Corrected source: frontend/src/debugHeaders.ts (revealFirstDebugHeaderError and validateDebugHeaders).
' Observed behavior: the pre-change frontend had no custom request-header controls and requestRaw generated X-HW-ID internally.
' Implemented architecture change: a development-only generic editor contributes one immutable Headers copy to the initial event POST.
' Product constraint: there are no credential modes, preset names, generated-header rows, annotations, or persistent storage.
' Security hardening: invalid names and values block submission; temporary headers never spread to history, configuration, or control requests.
' Design reason: a generic key-value surface supports fast protocol debugging without freezing current credential names into the UI.

title Internal debug header flow
left to right direction

actor "Developer" as Developer

rectangle "Internal development frontend" as DevFrontend {
  component "Headers panel\nKey-value rows and inline validation" as Panel
  component "In-memory enabled rows\nclear on reload" as HeaderState
  component "Initial event request adapter\nimmutable Headers copy" as EventAdapter
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Runtime V1" as Runtime {
  component "POST sessions/{sessionId}/events\nRuntimeEventController.submit" as Submit
  component "RuntimeRequestContext\nrecognized credential values" as Snapshot
  component "Agent execution context" as Execution
}

rectangle "mate-service" as Mate {
  component "Agent, Skill, and tool metadata\ndiscovery without credentials" as Discovery
  component "POST runtime/tools/{toolId}/execute\nrecognized credentials attached" as Execute
}

Developer --> Panel : edit temporary rows
Panel --> HeaderState : update enabled rows or clear
HeaderState --> EventAdapter : copy on message submit
EventAdapter --> Submit : initial event POST only
Submit --> Snapshot : read recognized request headers
Snapshot --> Execution : hold for this execution
Execution --> Discovery : discover tools
Execution --> Execute : invoke a selected tool

note bottom of Panel
No preset names or credential modes.
Keep one trailing blank row.
Generated headers are not rendered.
Manual values override generated values.

Reject invalid header names and values.
Reject case-insensitive duplicate custom names.
Apply the Fetch forbidden name-and-value algorithm.
Expand before focusing the exact invalid field.
end note

note bottom of EventAdapter
Never attach temporary headers to:
- Session create or read
- History, model, or thinking
- Steer, FollowUp, or Abort

Do not replay the event POST after disconnect.
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Runtime transport behavior:
- Read recognized values without authenticating them
- Do not persist values in Session or events
- Later edits affect only the next execution
- Ignore unrecognized values after the inbound request
end note

note bottom of Mate
Backend implementation behavior:
- Discovery receives no credential values
- Tool execute receives recognized credential values
- Missing required values fail before outbound call
- Logs and errors show presence only
end note
@enduml
